Z||000000||David DeVoe||10-13-2001||06:03 PM||||THis may sound dumb but is the coil used on the Fiero specific to the Fiero or is it a generic coil used on all 2.8 during the same time period. Im thinking of the wiring connections and mounting method specifically. I ask becaused looking in parts catalogs I rarely see any ignition stuff for the Fiero but always see it for Camaros etc. I would think that it would be generic. Anybody??????<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||10-13-2001||06:34 PM||||I have seen that particular ignition coil in a variety of GM cars that use the 2.8 V6. If you can find an aftermarket coil for the Camaro/Firebirds of those years it should have no problem fitting the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Capt Fiero||10-13-2001||07:01 PM||||Just get an MSD Blaster II coil it is a direct plug in for the fiero V6 MSD Part Number 8226<P>------------------<BR>David<BR>85GT<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://photos.onebigvillage.com/pubimage.asp?id_=32415"> ||||reg||1
